<article class="env-lemma" id="0EDG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EDG">Lemma <span data-tag="0EDG">72.18.4</span>.</a> In the situation of Definition <a href="/tag/0EDF" data-tag="0EDF">72.18.3</a> the intersection number $(\mathcal{L}_1 \cdots \mathcal{L}_ d \cdot Z)$ is an integer. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Any numerical polynomial of degree $e$ in $n_1, \ldots , n_ d$ can be written uniquely as a $\mathbf{Z}$-linear combination of the functions ${n_1 \choose k_1}{n_2 \choose k_2} \ldots {n_ d \choose k_ d}$ with $k_1 + \ldots + k_ d \leq e$. Apply this with $e = d$. Left as an exercise. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>